From ffa1c7d430799e591790b1fcebdf3bc46a935006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Mausberg <samuelmausberg@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:18:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Certified LM head: greedy plain decode

Behind SGLANG_CERTIFIED_HEAD_DECODE (off by default), the target head in
the decode CUDA graphs is computed by the verified-progress certified_head
package, imported from SGLANG_CERTIFIED_HEAD_SRC. Each graph captures the
certified head under a device flag and the stock head under its negation.
Before a replay the host sets the flag when the batch is all greedy and
needs no logits (no logprobs, penalties, logit bias, grammar, custom logit
processor, sampling mask, observer or beam rows). The certified ids are
copied out after the replay and replace the sampler's argmax. Undecided
rows run this engine's own BF16 head at the same shape, so the token is the
stock head's token for that batch. Eager forwards run the stock head.

SGLANG_CERTIFIED_HEAD_CHECK also runs the stock head in every certified step
and counts rows whose tokens differ; SGLANG_CERTIFIED_HEAD_STATS writes the
counters. Unsupported configurations (TP or PP > 1, DP attention, quantized,
LoRA, FP32, scaled or softcapped heads, padded vocabularies, NaN
sanitizing) log a warning and keep the stock head.
